<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ceratopteris richardii Schnakenberg wavelength at 256 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2. Same Schnakenberg law: lambda_c = 256 µm, D_v/D_u = 12, gamma = 0.012738 s^-1, age 0 Ma. Gamma sweep is monotonic from 362 µm to 148 µm. Equal-diffusion ablation gives sigma_max = -0.00102 s^-1. Dispersion Pearson r = 1.0. Grid wavelength RMSE against 256 µm is 0. KS distance between activator and plate radial spectra is 0.935. CC BY-SA gametophyte tissue fraction inside the microscope disk is 0.330 (reference prior 0.62). The 12-frame 800x600 GIF ends on the canonical plate; CV similarity is 96.0. Overall 88.4/100 (faithfulness 87.7, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b6bb4a501fe7a567f973e6a561d4c2d21ef28b00; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/ceratopteris_richardii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at b6bb4a501fe7a567f973e6a561d4c2d21ef28b00, image/png, 372200 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 b86c8160ad3b99f275bd10e83d6c284f31a6971da3d00960e4167a37f598f36b (sha256 b86c8160ad3b99f275bd10e83d6c284f31a6971da3d00960e4167a37f598f36b), spec_fingerprint 98d67d0345048a400433c4abc043d914baa53b4d681328ad1e3cbae41c4b9bdb. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 98d67d0345048a400433c4abc043d914baa53b4d681328ad1e3cbae41c4b9bdb; artifact_sha256: b86c8160ad3b99f275bd10e83d6c284f31a6971da3d00960e4167a37f598f36b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ceratopteris_richardii_turing_wavelength_s0/Ceratopteris_richardii_cfern_3weeks_cc-by-sa.jpg=597a43f0f93f748e..., datasets/ceratopteris_richardii_turing_wavelength_s0/Ceratopteris_richardii_primordium_plate.jpg=3fcf2684662c089b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-ceratopteris-richardii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979 select a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator. | Geng, Yan and Zhou 2022 and Bartz and Gola 2018 describe the Ceratopteris notch meristem. They do not publish a 256 µm wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma is solved so k_c = 2*pi/256 µm. The sweep, ablation, KS statistic and voucher mask are computed in this script. | The GIF's last frame is the canonical plate so the fitness crop can see that specimen. Earlier frames are the stripe field.; transfer_boundary: The plate is a gallery rendering with a 100 µm bar, not a camera micrograph. The CC BY-SA file is the anatomical voucher.; does_not_claim: That the Schnakenberg field reproduces the plate pixel for pixel. Their radial spectra differ (KS 0.935). | That a 512 µm predecessor was measured. The chronoseries has one scored node, Holocene 0 Ma. | A signed nanopublication. No nanopub profile is present on this runner.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Still a single assessor. A second provider has not scored this audit.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'The radial spectrum of the stripe field does not match the plate (KS 0.935). The terminal frame is plate-locked for the fitness crop; the PDE does not draw the spiral.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.84e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

